

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 10

                                  FOR

                                PROMETEO







          Andrea Giovannetti
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  Elizabeth I, Queen of England, to her subjects in 1601:
  "You have had, and may have, many mightier and wiser princes sitting upon 
this throne; yet you never had, nor shall have any that will love you 
better."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  In spring, Prometeo travelled to Mongu.

  Soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the Uga-Buga Makumb (#1)ian 
empire marched on the Jungle province of Plumwood, a land garrisoned by the 
forces of Prometeo.  Uga-Buga Makumb's forces experienced little resistance 
in Plumwood and Uga-Buga Makumb there established our reign.  
Uga-Buga Makumb leads approximately 1 Bowmen, 2 Legion, 2 Chariots, 3 
Dragons and 2 Trolls.
  During early summer, Prometeo rode into Macondo.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded the province of Tesawa, a 
Mountain area ruled by Prometeo.  Tesawa was overrun and occupied by Pascal 
(#78)'s host.  Pascal leads approximately 2 Legion and 2 Chariots.
  In late summer, Prometeo was instructed in Sageness by Indra.  Prometeo 
practiced his Sageness and improved noticeably.  He invented nothing in his 
sagely experiments.

  A fleet sent by the empire of Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) 
invaded Waterford, hoping to subjugate that province ruled by Prometeo and 
made up of extensive Seas.  Tlazolteotl (#88)'s forces experienced little 
opposition in Waterford and Tlazolteotl there established our reign.  
Tlazolteotl leads approximately 3 Phalanx and 5 Dragons.
  With the coming of the fall season, Prometeo was tutored in Sageness by 
Ishtar.  Prometeo practiced enthusiastically and improved his ability in 
Sageness.  He invented nothing worthy of note in his sagely researches.
  The fall darkened into a frigid early winter.  Prometeo was tutored in 
Sageness by Ishtar.  Prometeo tried to improve his Sageness, but the task 
was beyond his natural ability.  His experience raised his aptitude in 
Sageness.  He discovered nothing in his sagely researches.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Prometeo for this year.


  Prometeo treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Prometeo treated with his 
ally Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Prometeo treated with his ally Hokuto (#4).
Prometeo treated with his ally II Kahn (#6).  Prometeo treated with his ally 
Giovanna (#7).  Prometeo treated with his ally Circe (#8).  Prometeo treated 
with his ally Agesilao (#9).

  Here is the financial report for Prometeo's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 2 gold in revenue.  8 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  0 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Prometeo was left 
with 49 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Marlon
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season I prepared to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  Illegal command.
  Windy spring was followed by early summer.  Illegal command.
  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) invaded the province of Alderwood, a 
Forest area ruled by Prometeo.  Teleko (#72) commanded the invading armies.  
The defenders were led by me.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle 
as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Alderwood (0101):

  319th     321st     322nd   
  Eagles    Eagles    Eagles  
 ооо01ооо  ооо01ооо  ооо01ооо 
                              
 326th/A   323rd/V   320th/C  
 Dragons    Trolls    Eagles  
 01  ддд01ддд  ооо01ооо 
------------------------------
 ннн05ннн  ннн05ннн  ннн05ннн 
 258th/V   232nd/A   257th/C  
  Legion    Legion    Legion  
                              
  DEFENDING ARMY

  Standing tall with his warriors was Teleko.  I stood determinedly at the 
head of my thousands.
  The battle was a fair fight, as no luck of great importance seemed to 
influence the overall result of the engagement before it started.  Tactical 
supremacy was clearly guaranteed by Teleko's powerful tactical mind.

  Out on the right outside flank, the 326th Dragons were arrayed against the 
Veteran 258th Legion.  The 326th Dragons soared over the 258th Legion and 
attacked them.  The 319th Eagles swooped down on the 258th Legion and 
attacked without mercy.  On this battleground, the clever commander of the 
326th Dragons thought of an idea.  He dragged a few monks out of a nearby 
monastery and lined them up as human shields.  The 326th Dragons fought with 
the 258th Legion and determinedly plowed into their opponents.
  In the interior lines, the Veteran 323rd Trolls were arrayed against the 
232nd Legion.  The 321st Eagles soared over the 232nd Legion and attacked 
without mercy.  The 323rd Trolls battled with the 232nd Legion and viciously 
crushed them.
  Out on the left outside wing, the Crack 320th Eagles were encouraged to 
fanatical anger by Teleko, their glorious Ace of Eagles.  They were arrayed 
against the Crack 257th Legion.  The 320th Eagles soared over the 257th 
Legion and attacked them.  The 322nd Eagles swooped down on the 257th Legion 
and attacked them.  In this sector, a few soldiers of the 257th Legion 
panicked; however, they were quickly executed by roving security police, and 
the battle proceeded with little disruption.  It seemed that the 320th 
Eagles would break through and win.
  But the battle was not yet done.  The 320th Eagles carelessly blundered 
into a nest of booby traps and lost some of their best front-line troops.  
Even so, the 320th Eagles battled the 257th Legion and was able to make some 
progress.
  The host of Teleko broke the army of Prometeo's fighting spirit with one 
last, great push.  The 326th Dragons scattered the 258th Legion in all 
directions.  The 323rd Trolls annihilated the 232nd Legion.  The 320th 
Eagles slew the 257th Legion almost to a man.
  Alderwood was overrun by Teleko's forces in a bloody campaign.  My forces 
completely destroyed, I escaped alone to Mare Imbrium.
  Midsummer's night came and went and late summer arrived.  Illegal command.
  In fall, Illegal command.
  During early winter, Marlon's Bless spell backfired and I wound up covered 
with psycho-kinetic slime.
  Speaking with friendly adventurers, I learned a rumor about a previously 
unknown Hollow Tree in Alderwood (#101), held by the Dryad, who according to 
legend possesses the Reflector of Armies.

  Thy humble servant,   Marlon


From: Tonto, Squire to Ishtar
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Stormy winter gave way to spring, and Ishtar prepared to carry out his 
imperial orders.  He tried to improve his Sageness, but the task was beyond 
his natural aptitude.  In his sagely researches, he discovered a fabulous 
invention called the Hand-Held Radar!  The following benefits are conferred 
by the Hand-Held Radar:
  Hand-Held Radar sets are distributed to all characters employed by the 
Kingdom.  They enable characters to find features regardless of whether a 
Hide Feature spell has been cast on the feature by an Illusionist.

  Rainulf (#25)'s Kill Enemy spell backfired and Rainulf wound up with his 
face covered with psycho-kinetic slime.
  With the coming of the early summer season, Ishtar tried to practice his 
Sageness, but the task seemed beyond his natural aptitude.  He discovered 
nothing in his sagely researches.
  With the coming of the late summer season Ishtar tried a Resurrection 
spell, but botched it.
  The summer mellowed into the fall.  Ishtar tried to improve his Sageness, 
but the task was beyond his aptitude.  He invented nothing in his sagely 
experiments.
  With the advent of the early winter season, Ishtar tried to improve his 
Sageness, but the task was beyond his ability.  He discovered nothing 
valuable in his sagely researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Tonto, Squire to Ishtar


From: Berthier, Squire to Girard
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season Girard set out to quench his thirst 
for adventure.  He moved into Cantia.  Girard observed the terrain while we 
were on the march and now 100% of Cantia has been explored.  Girard also 
found a Dungeon (#82) in Cantia, occupied by the Werewolf.  What treasure 
may lie there is unknown.  Those who stalk the night fear the Werewolf, a 
man with the ability to turn into a wolfman or even a full wolf.  According 
to legend, he who is severely bitten by the werewolf is cursed to become one 
himself.  Girard saw no monsters.
  In early summer, Girard journeyed to St Helens.  Northeast of here lies 
the province of Cherrywood (#501), ruled by 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  It is known to be a Forest province 
inhabited by Humans.  Their Human warriors prefer to fight as Bowmen and 
Light Cavalry.  Viewing the eastern horizon, one can see a Mountain province 
known as Silvermist (#502).  It is said that 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll reigns there.  It is known to be occupied 
by Eagles.  If need be, they can muster an army of Eagles to defend their 
territory.  While adventuring, Girard saw no monster.
  With the advent of the late summer season, Girard travelled to Amberleaf.  
To the north lay an icy wasteland which extends as far as a man can see.  
While adventuring, Girard saw no wandering monster.
  The sultry days of summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  Girard explored 
Amberleaf and now 23% of it has been explored.  His experience raised his 
skill in Exploring.  In his travels, he saw no monsters.
  During early winter, Girard explored Amberleaf thoroughly, leaving no 
stone unturned, and our exploration level there has risen to 53%.  Girard 
encountered no marauding monsters.
  Girard heard a rumor telling of a feature in the El Kalaa Sea (#201), an 
Ancient Megaliths inhabited by the Werewolf.  The Ancient Megaliths is 
reputed to contain the Large Hoard of Gold.

  Thy humble servant,   Berthier, Squire to Girard


